-- Golomb upper-bound record V012 — validity.
-- Each table entry is an explicit ruler, given as a list and checked by the kernel with V007's
-- `rulerCheck` (distinct marks, the length is a mark, every mark is at most the length, all
-- pairwise sums distinct via a `Nat` bitset), through V007's `f_le_of_rulerCheck`. The rulers
-- are data; no search happens here. The `if` chain of `small` is discharged by a
-- chain of `by_cases`, as in V007 (`split_ifs` is far too expensive on such a chain).

namespace SqueezeBench.Golomb.Upper.V012

open SqueezeBench
open SqueezeBench.Golomb.Upper.V007 (f_le_of_rulerCheck)

